# RLS + PgBouncer Harness

## Status
VERIFIED — docker route passes `test_pgbouncer_leak.sh` twice (2026-11-07).

## Author Local Commands
Native user-space route (no Docker needed):
```bash
cd /path/to/repo
tools/env/up.sh
make test-01
```

Docker route (isolated project `nexo-s01`, ports 15431/16431 — distinct
from the native env's 15432/16432):
```bash
cd samples/01-rls-pgbouncer/harness
docker compose up -d
NEXO_PGBOUNCER_PORT=16431 bash test_pgbouncer_leak.sh
docker compose down -v
```

## What it tests
1. Session-level setting leaking between PgBouncer connections
2. SET LOCAL preventing the leak with transaction pooling
3. RLS default-deny with no tenant context and cross-tenant reads
